title: Campaigning
new-page: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1
max-visits: 36
is-card: true
card-image: img/media_1.png
frequency: 100
tags: party_affairs

= Campaigning

[? if npp_party_chair == "Remma" : Make friends. Be natural. <span class="tooltip-new">You've<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Remma.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ remma_description +]</span></span> always advocated for low profile but consistent campaigns. <span class="tooltip-new">Macalintal<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Macalintal.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ macalintal_description +]</span></span> interrupts your train of thought as he shows us another opportunity to spread our word. You tell him that you feel egotistic just heading this. He asks if you think you’re not ready for it. The air rushes out of your lungs. ?]
[? if npp_party_chair == "Clueless" : Same old schedules. Same old strategies. There’s eventually a point where <span class="tooltip-new">you're<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Clueless.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ clueless_description +]</span></span> tired of it all. Again and again your calendar is dotted out with the same schedules. You still feel that passion inside of you, but it's exhausting to show up to these things in the first place. Nobody gets shit done fast enough without you sometimes. As you lay down in your bed staring at the ceiling, <span class="tooltip-new">Macalintal<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Macalintal.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ macalintal_description +]</span></span> and <span class="tooltip-new">Remma<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Remma.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ remma_description +]</span></span> interrupt. Another event we can hold. “Where can we go?” ?]
[? if npp_party_chair == "Ka San" : Your ass hurts as the ride back to HQ is with a rapidly moving jeepney. <span class="tooltip-new">Macalintal<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Macalintal.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ macalintal_description +]</span></span> and <span class="tooltip-new">Clueless<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Clueless.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ clueless_description +]</span></span> are beside <span class="tooltip-new">you<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/KaSan.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ kasan_description +]</span></span> as they discuss more events to hold. The revolutionary and violent future you’ve always hoped for shouldn't probably look like this. You should be thinking about shooting <span class="tooltip-new">Yuuto<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Yuuto.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ yuuto_description +]</span></span> and <span class="tooltip-new">Blooky<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Blooky.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ blooky_description +]</span></span> in the head. As the ride continues on your way home from the rally, your busmates talk about another one. “Santi, where do we go next?” ?]
[? if npp_party_chair == "Robbie" : A picture of <span class="tooltip-new">Remma<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Remma.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ remma_description +]</span></span>, our former <span class="tooltip-new">Chancellor<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Chancellor.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ chancellor_description +]</span></span>, the old cabinet, and <span class="tooltip-new">you<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Robbie.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ barnabus_description +]</span></span> sits on the desk. You’re alone for a while before the former shows up. We’re gonna do the usual anyway, put up some posters, edit some paragraphs, then publish them all in the hopes of better poll numbers. Usually, you have fun doing these types of things. There’s something different today. You ask Remma if this planning session would be happier if we had them by our side. He doesn't answer, but he’s shaken to the core. You weep. ?]
[? if npp_party_chair == "Macalintal" : Get the ball rolling. That’s what <span class="tooltip-new">you've<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Macalintal.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ macalintal_description +]</span></span>, always been saying, as long as we start early we’ll be able to jump up our results. <span class="tooltip-new">Remma<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Remma.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ remma_description +]</span></span>, interrupts your musings as he talks about how there's a free opportunity to hold a campaign, those meet-and-greets whatever. You tell him that you’ve never felt like it was right for you to be the one going out for this. He replies that you’re the chairperson anyway. He trusts you to make decisions. Do you? ?]
[? if npp_party_chair == "Shooter" : Ever since you’ve come into the scene, you’ve always pushed for the NPP to gather more casually and closely. No more of those LARP agreements whatever, you gotta act tough for the cameras. This time, you’re in a bar as <span class="tooltip-new">Remma<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Remma.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ remma_description +]</span></span> and <span class="tooltip-new">Santi<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/KaSan.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ kasan_description +]</span></span> talk to you about our next event. Before you order another round, Santi asks you if you’ll slip up and say that word again before she laughs. Remma ignores her at the side, and tells you that he’ll be with you at your next destination. ?]
[? if npp_party_chair == "Naomi" : You’ve always hated showing yourself off to others. At least that’s what you’ve convinced yourself to believe. As you sit with <span class="tooltip-new">Remma<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Remma.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ remma_description +]</span></span> discussing your next places to campaign, you just wish for a place where you can be yourself and be accepted. <span class="tooltip-new">Naomi<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Naomi.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ naomi_description +]</span></span> hate it when you feel like you’re only taken seriously with a mask on. Remma snaps you out of your thinking, and asks if you’re willing to go to one more event. You ask him if they’ll like you. He doesn’t tell you anything that you could have told yourself. He asks you to believe, to have faith. ?]
[? if npp_party_chair == "Danni" : What to do. What to do. <span class="tooltip-new">You<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Paisco.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ paisco_description +]</span></span> were never sure when you took up this position in the first place. The only thing you can think about is if you’ll do something wrong. You're scared of messing up, of doing nothing. <span class="tooltip-new">Remma<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Remma.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ remma_description +]</span></span> assures you that you’re a good person, but what does it mean when you can’t do anything at all? The list of potential places Remma shows you looks like a word search, you can’t decipher any of these terms. But you have the energy to at least try. ?]
[? if npp_party_chair == "Ka Fil" : All these exercises, all these events, it’s all <span class="tooltip-new">your<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/KaFil.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ kafil_description +]</span></span> calling. You’re the expert in getting people riled up. You’re the expert in making things look funny, appealing, and strong. <span class="tooltip-new">Remma<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Remma.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ remma_description +]</span></span> and <span class="tooltip-new">Macalintal<span class="tooltiptext"><img src="img/portraits/Macalintal.png" alt="Leader"><br>[+ macalintal_description +]</span></span> come over for the usual, asking you to do these things for the party. Is that all you’re good for??]

- @workers
- @new_middle
- @old_middle
- @rural
- @unemployed
- @davao_campaign
- @discard_campaign
- @return_campaign

@workers
title: We can always try with the urban working class, they're our people.
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: workers_npp += 6*(1-dissent); workers_npp -= 2 if unemployed >= 15; workers_npp -= 2 if unemployed >= 25;  resources -= 1; workers_npp += 3*(1-dissent) if nationalization_progress >= 1;

<div class="container">
<div class="image"><img src="img/event/labor_2.png"></div>
<div class="text">We have increased our campaigning among the workers. [? if unemployed < 15: Our traditional base is with us all the way in fighting the enemies of the proletariat. ?][? if unemployed >= 15: The high levels of unemployment make our campaign more difficult, with some people calling us insensitive. ?]</div></div>

@new_middle
title: Why can't we work with the intelligentsia? We came from there, we can negotiate.
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: new_middle_npp += 6*(1-dissent); new_middle_npp -= 4 if socialism <= 49; resources -= 1;

<div class="container">
<div class="image"><img src="img/event/labor_1.png"></div>
<div class="text">We have increased our campaigning among the new middle class. [? if socialism <= 49 : The popular antipathy towards socialism among this group makes our campaign more difficult. ?] [? if socialism > 49: With our new inroads, we have an easier time increasing support among the middle class than before. ?]</div></div>

@old_middle
title: The middle class, despite its elitist roots, cannot be ignored. I'll have to harden my heart and ring up some landlords.
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: old_middle_npp += 5*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; old_middle_npp -= 3 if authoritarianism >= 51

<div class="container">
<div class="image"><img src="img/event/labor_1.png"></div>
<div class="text">We have increased our campaigning among the old middle class. [? if nationalism >= 51: The high levels of nationalism among this group make our campaign more difficult. ?] [? if nationalism < 51: With anti-authorianism spreading, we have an easier time increasing support among the middle class than before. ?]</div></div>

@rural
title: Peasants and farmers have always been our type, we just haven't reached out to them enough.
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: rural_npp += 5*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; rural_npp += 3*(1-dissent) if rural_policy >= 2

<div class="container">
<div class="image"><img src="img/event/farmer_1.png"></div>
<div class="text">We have increased our campaigning among farmers. [? if rural_policy < 2: We have not historically campaigned much among the farmers, and they do not trust us. ?][? if rural_policy >= 2 : Our rural policies have made it easier for us to build support among farmers. ?]</div></div>

@unemployed
title: Unemployed citizens are always the ones who get the short end of the stick. We have to show that we care, that we try.
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: unemployed_npp += 6*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; unemployed_npp -= 3 if welfare < 0; unemployed_npp += 6*(1-dissent) if new_deal_adopted = 1; unemployed_npp += 3*(1-dissent) if welfare >= 2;

<div class="container">
<div class="image"><img src="img/event/sad_citizen_1.png"></div>
<div class="text">We have increased our campaigning among the unemployed. [? if welfare < 0: The welfare cuts and resultant poverty make our campaign more difficult, since we are associated with the government that enacted these cuts, and our campaign may even backfire. ?]</div></div>

@davao_campaign
title: We have to talk to Davao at some point, let's schedule a rally.
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
view-if: peoples_party == 1
on-arrival: catholics_npp += 6*(1-dissent); resources -= 1

<div class="container">
<div class="image"><img src="img/event/blooky.png"></div>
<div class="text">We have increased our campaigning among Davaoenos. Although their main representation lies in the AMDG, we can sap some of their voters away.</div></div>

@discard_campaign
title: But we can't campaign right now, let's try next time.
subtitle: Discard card.
go-to: root

@return_campaign
title: This isn't that much of a priority, let's just come back later?
subtitle: Return to hand.
go-to: easy_discard